# Contacts. Run the requests top to bottom: later ones use the id created by "createContact".
# Docs: docs/contacts.md

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5033
@missingId = 999999

### List contacts: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts

### Create a contact: 201 with a Location header
# @name createContact
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ana",
  "phone": "+50761234567"
}

### Get the created contact: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/{{createContact.response.body.$.id}}

### Update the created contact: 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/{{createContact.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ana María",
  "phone": "+50769876543"
}

### Delete the created contact: 204 (409 if it has messages)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/{{createContact.response.body.$.id}}

### --- Errors ---

### Invalid body: 400 with errors for Name and Phone
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "phone": "abc"
}

### Contact that doesn't exist: 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/{{missingId}}

### Update a contact that doesn't exist: 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/{{missingId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Nadie",
  "phone": "+50760000001"
}

### Non-numeric id: 404 (the route only accepts numbers)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/contacts/abc
